{
  "$comment": [
    "Two halves. The DAEMON is a separate long-lived process — a LaunchAgent, or",
    "`a2a-serve` in a terminal — and is NOT started by this file: an inbound",
    "listener has to outlive any one client, which a client-spawned stdio server",
    "cannot. See the README.",
    "",
    "Every client here needs the SAME A2A_TOKEN as the daemon, and must leave",
    "A2A_STATE_DIR alone so both halves resolve the same store.",
    "",
    "For the claude/channel push, start Claude Code with",
    "  claude --dangerously-load-development-channels server:a2a",
    "and confirm the dialog. Do NOT also pass --channels for the same entry: the",
    "bypass is per-entry and the --channels copy is refused as not on the",
    "allowlist. In -p mode nothing is delivered at all, which looks like a bug",
    "and is not one — use a2a_wait_for_task there."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "a2a": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcp-a2a/dist/cli.js"],
      "env": {
        "A2A_DAEMON_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:41241",
        "A2A_TOKEN": "the same value the daemon was started with",
        "A2A_ALLOW_WRITES": ""
      }
    }
  }
}
